            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In confined spaces, marginally — it needs 4 degrees of swing instead of 5. But the finer teeth are smaller and the mechanism more delicate, so a well-made 72-tooth ratchet outperforms a cheap 90-tooth one. The big jump is from 36 to 72; after that the returns diminish quickly."
          }
