          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Seventy-two teeth suits most people: a 5-degree swing handles the overwhelming majority of tight spots while keeping the teeth substantial. Move to 90 if you regularly work in engine bays or machinery. Stay at 36 if your access is generally open and you value robustness."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
