            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Each tooth is smaller, with less material at its base and less depth for the pawl to engage, so under very high torque a fine-tooth ratchet is more likely to skip. Good manufacturers offset this with better steel and pawl design, but a cheap high-count ratchet has the fine teeth without that compensation."
          }
