        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tooth count sets your swing arc and nothing else: <strong class="text-white">360 divided by the count</strong>. The meaningful upgrade is escaping the low numbers — 36 to 72 halves the swing. Past that you are buying one degree at a time while the mechanism gets finer and more fragile.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Seventy-two teeth from a good maker beats ninety from a cheap one.</strong> And keep the high-torque work off the ratchet entirely: a breaker bar has no mechanism to skip, which is why the people who own both rarely damage either.
          </p>
